{
  "title": "E se a lanterna só acendesse em pacotes?",
  "setting": "Uma praça ao entardecer",
  "mission": "Descubra com seus amigos como a luz da lanterna da feira se comporta: em **pacotes, ondas ou os dois?**",
  "deadline": null,
  "panels": [],
  "team": [
    {
      "id": "amiga",
      "role": "Amiga curiosa",
      "expertise": "Gosta de testar ideias malucas e fazer experiências",
      "ai": false
    },
    {
      "id": "amigo",
      "role": "Amigo observador",
      "expertise": "Presta atenção em detalhes e gosta de contar coisas",
      "ai": false
    }
  ],
  "meters": [
    {
      "id": "clareza",
      "label": "Clareza do que está acontecendo",
      "start": 20,
      "goodWhen": "high"
    }
  ],
  "skills": [
    {
      "id": "pacotes",
      "name": "Energia vem em pacotes",
      "practice": "Explique em uma frase para alguém por que a luz não pode chegar em qualquer quantidade."
    },
    {
      "id": "dualidade",
      "name": "Dualidade onda-partícula",
      "practice": "Use uma lanterna e uma fresta para observar como a luz faz faixas e também chega em pacotes."
    }
  ],
  "startNodeId": "inicio",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "inicio",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "amiga",
          "text": "A lanterna da feira acendeu, mas saiu um clarão e depois tudo escuro. A luz parece que vem em tijolos!"
        },
        {
          "from": "amigo",
          "text": "Se a luz fosse contínua, dava para dosar. Mas ela insiste em vir só em pacotes."
        }
      ],
      "prompt": "O que você tenta fazer para entender a lanterna?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "cobrir-metade",
          "text": "Cobrir metade da lanterna com a mão e ver se sai meio pacote",
          "quality": "weak",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "amigo",
              "text": "A luz não quis sair pela metade: ou sai o pacote inteiro, ou não sai. É isso que chamam de quantum."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "clareza",
              "change": -5
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "pacotes",
              "kind": "improve",
              "text": "Você tentou dividir um pacote, mas a energia vem em quantidades inteiras. Cobrir a metade não dividiu o pacote.",
              "example": "“A luz pode ser fraca, mas cada pacote é inteiro: não existe meio pacote.”"
            }
          ],
          "next": "fresta"
        },
        {
          "id": "usar-fresta",
          "text": "Fazer a luz passar por uma fresta estreita entre dois cadernos",
          "quality": "strong",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "amiga",
              "text": "A fresta não dividiu o pacote, mas a luz se espalhou do outro lado, como uma onda na água."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "clareza",
              "change": 10
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "dualidade",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "Você deixou a luz passar por uma fresta e observou o que ela faz. A luz mostrou um lado de onda.",
              "example": null
            }
          ],
          "next": "fresta"
        },
        {
          "id": "apontar-longe",
          "text": "Apontar a lanterna para longe e ver se o pacote se divide",
          "quality": "fair",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "amigo",
              "text": "A luz continuou em pacotes lá longe. Boa ideia, mas o feixe não se divide assim."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "clareza",
              "change": 5
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "pacotes",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "Você testou se os pacotes se dividiam no caminho. É um jeito de investigar em vez de só acreditar.",
              "example": null
            }
          ],
          "next": "fresta"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fresta",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "amiga",
          "text": "A mancha na parede mostra faixas claras e escuras, mas também uns pontinhos separados."
        },
        {
          "from": "amigo",
          "text": "Isso parece onda e partícula ao mesmo tempo. Por onde a gente começa?"
        }
      ],
      "prompt": "O que você faz para decidir o que a luz é?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "ver-os-dois",
          "text": "Observar as faixas e os pontinhos juntos, aproximando e afastando a fresta",
          "quality": "strong",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "amiga",
              "text": "Você viu as faixas que são coisa de onda e os pontinhos que chegam um por um. A luz é as duas coisas!"
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "clareza",
              "change": 30
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "dualidade",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "Você olhou para os dois comportamentos da luz ao mesmo tempo: as faixas de onda e os pacotes de partícula.",
              "example": null
            }
          ],
          "next": "entendeu"
        },
        {
          "id": "so-pontos",
          "text": "Contar só os pontinhos um por um e anotar quantos aparecem",
          "quality": "fair",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "amigo",
              "text": "Os pacotes são reais, mas você deixou de olhar as faixas. Faltou ver o lado onda."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "clareza",
              "change": 10
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "dualidade",
              "kind": "improve",
              "text": "Você descreveu só metade da história. A luz também forma faixas quando passa por uma fresta.",
              "example": "“Vejo pacotes, mas por que a luz também faz ondas na parede?”"
            }
          ],
          "next": "so-particula"
        },
        {
          "id": "usar-celular",
          "text": "Guardar a lanterna da feira e usar a lanterna do celular, que é contínua",
          "quality": "weak",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "amiga",
              "text": "A do celular também é luz, mas você não aproveitou para entender a da feira."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "clareza",
              "change": -10
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "pacotes",
              "kind": "improve",
              "text": "Trocar de lanterna resolveu a pressa, mas não a curiosidade. A luz do celular também chega em pacotes, só que pequenos demais para a gente notar.",
              "example": null
            }
          ],
          "next": "desistiu"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "endings": [
    {
      "id": "entendeu",
      "outcome": "Vocês entenderam que a luz da lanterna é onda e partícula ao mesmo tempo. A clareza da turma subiu para 60."
    },
    {
      "id": "so-particula",
      "outcome": "Vocês viram os pacotes, mas esqueceram as ondas. A clareza subiu um pouco, mas a dúvida continuou."
    },
    {
      "id": "desistiu",
      "outcome": "Você usou o celular e seguiu o passeio, mas a pergunta da lanterna ficou no ar. Na próxima, dá para investigar sem pressa."
    }
  ],
  "summary": [
    "A energia da luz chega em pacotes inteiros, não em qualquer quantidade.",
    "Quando a luz passa por uma fresta, ela forma faixas de onda e também aparece em pacotes: as duas coisas juntas."
  ]
}

{
  "title": "Does the new dressing really lower infections?",
  "setting": "Day 3 at Lakeside Clinic",
  "mission": "Decide whether the new antimicrobial dressing truly lowers infection rates before the unit changes practice. **Test the gap between 6 infections out of 40 and 2 out of 38.**",
  "deadline": "Meeting with {{manager}} today at 3 p.m.",
  "panels": [
    {
      "title": "Infection rates by dressing protocol",
      "metrics": [
        {
          "label": "Standard dressing",
          "value": "40 patients, 6 infections",
          "note": "15.0%"
        },
        {
          "label": "New dressing",
          "value": "38 patients, 2 infections",
          "note": "5.3%"
        },
        {
          "label": "Difference",
          "value": "9.7 points",
          "note": "Could be chance"
        }
      ],
      "note": "Three months of data; a chi-square test would give p ≈ 0.08."
    }
  ],
  "team": [
    {
      "id": "manager",
      "role": "Nurse manager",
      "expertise": "Wants a decision today; worries about staff time and costs.",
      "ai": false
    },
    {
      "id": "icn",
      "role": "Infection control nurse",
      "expertise": "Knows how to compare infection rates; careful about sample size.",
      "ai": false
    },
    {
      "id": "charge",
      "role": "Charge nurse",
      "expertise": "Has seen both protocols on the floor; wants what's best for patients.",
      "ai": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ai",
      "role": "AI assistant",
      "expertise": "Runs calculations and checks numbers when asked.",
      "ai": true
    }
  ],
  "meters": [
    {
      "id": "risk",
      "label": "Risk of a wrong call",
      "start": 50,
      "goodWhen": "low"
    },
    {
      "id": "confidence",
      "label": "Confidence in the result",
      "start": 30,
      "goodWhen": "high"
    }
  ],
  "skills": [
    {
      "id": "chance",
      "name": "Tell a real difference from chance",
      "practice": "Explain what a p-value of 0.08 means to a colleague in one sentence."
    },
    {
      "id": "sample",
      "name": "Choose a sample size",
      "practice": "Use an online calculator to find the sample size needed to detect a 5-point difference in infection rates."
    },
    {
      "id": "explain",
      "name": "Explain a test result",
      "practice": "Explain the 3-month infection numbers to your nurse manager in plain words without saying 'p-value'."
    }
  ],
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "start",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "manager",
          "text": "The new dressing looks great—only 2 infections out of 38, vs. 6 out of 40. Can we switch today? I need an answer for the 3 p.m. staff meeting."
        },
        {
          "from": "icn",
          "text": "Hold on. 38 patients is not many. How do we know this gap isn't just luck from a small sample?"
        },
        {
          "from": "charge",
          "text": "I've tried both on the floor. The new one is easier and patients complain less, but is it truly safer?"
        }
      ],
      "prompt": "What do you do first?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "ask-ai",
          "text": "Ask {{ai}} to run a hypothesis test on the infection rates.",
          "quality": "strong",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "ai",
              "text": "I ran a chi-square test. The p-value is 0.08. That means a gap this big could happen by chance about 8 times in 100 if the dressings were actually the same."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "risk",
              "change": -20
            },
            {
              "meter": "confidence",
              "change": 20
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "chance",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "You checked whether the gap could be chance before acting.",
              "example": null
            }
          ],
          "next": "ai-result"
        },
        {
          "id": "switch-now",
          "text": "Recommend switching to the new dressing this week.",
          "quality": "weak",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "manager",
              "text": "Great, let's start. I'll tell the team."
            },
            {
              "from": "icn",
              "text": "But the sample is so small. What if it's just noise? We could be changing for nothing."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "risk",
              "change": 25
            },
            {
              "meter": "confidence",
              "change": -10
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "chance",
              "kind": "improve",
              "text": "You acted on a small sample without testing whether the gap could be chance.",
              "example": "One month of extra data would tell us more."
            }
          ],
          "next": "ending-early"
        },
        {
          "id": "wait-month",
          "text": "Suggest we wait one more month and collect more patients.",
          "quality": "fair",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "manager",
              "text": "We can wait, but I want a clear answer by then. Don't just kick the can."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "risk",
              "change": -10
            },
            {
              "meter": "confidence",
              "change": 5
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": {
            "label": "One month later",
            "panel": {
              "title": "Infection rates after one more month",
              "metrics": [
                {
                  "label": "Standard dressing",
                  "value": "70 patients, 7 infections",
                  "note": "10.0%"
                },
                {
                  "label": "New dressing",
                  "value": "65 patients, 4 infections",
                  "note": "6.2%"
                }
              ],
              "note": "Gap is only 3.8 points; p ≈ 0.45, still could be chance."
            }
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "sample",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "Waiting for more data is a fair move when the sample is small.",
              "example": null
            }
          ],
          "next": "after-wait"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ai-result",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "ai",
          "text": "The p-value is 0.08. That's above the usual 0.05 cutoff, so the evidence isn't strong enough to say the new dressing is better."
        },
        {
          "from": "icn",
          "text": "Exactly. With 0.08, we can't rule out chance. We'd need a bigger sample to see if this gap is real."
        },
        {
          "from": "manager",
          "text": "So what do I tell the staff? We have to decide something today."
        }
      ],
      "prompt": "What do you do with this information?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "ask-sample-size",
          "text": "Ask {{ai}} how many more patients we'd need to be sure.",
          "quality": "strong",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "ai",
              "text": "To have an 80% chance of detecting a drop from 10% to 4%, you'd need about 150 patients per group. At your current pace, that's 4 more months."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "risk",
              "change": -10
            },
            {
              "meter": "confidence",
              "change": 15
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "sample",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "You asked for the sample size needed before deciding.",
              "example": null
            }
          ],
          "next": "sample-size"
        },
        {
          "id": "explain-wait",
          "text": "Explain to {{manager}} that the evidence isn't strong enough and suggest one more month of data.",
          "quality": "fair",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "manager",
              "text": "Fine, one more month. But this better be the last delay."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "risk",
              "change": -5
            },
            {
              "meter": "confidence",
              "change": 5
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": {
            "label": "One month later",
            "panel": {
              "title": "Infection rates after one more month",
              "metrics": [
                {
                  "label": "Standard dressing",
                  "value": "70 patients, 7 infections",
                  "note": "10.0%"
                },
                {
                  "label": "New dressing",
                  "value": "65 patients, 4 infections",
                  "note": "6.2%"
                }
              ],
              "note": "Gap is 3.8 points; p ≈ 0.45."
            }
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "explain",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "You told the manager the evidence wasn't strong enough without jargon.",
              "example": "You said 'the gap could be chance' instead of 'p = 0.08'."
            }
          ],
          "next": "after-wait"
        },
        {
          "id": "adopt-anyway",
          "text": "Recommend adopting the new dressing because 2 infections is clearly less than 6.",
          "quality": "weak",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "icn",
              "text": "But the p-value says it could be chance. We shouldn't ignore that."
            },
            {
              "from": "manager",
              "text": "I like the lower number, but {{icn}} makes a good point."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "risk",
              "change": 20
            },
            {
              "meter": "confidence",
              "change": -10
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "chance",
              "kind": "improve",
              "text": "You ignored the p-value and treated a small, uncertain difference as proof.",
              "example": "A p-value of 0.08 means we need more evidence, not a decision."
            }
          ],
          "next": "ending-early"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "after-wait",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "manager",
          "text": "Okay, we waited. Now 70 vs. 65 patients, 7 vs. 4 infections. Is that enough to switch?"
        },
        {
          "from": "icn",
          "text": "The gap is only 3.8 points, and a quick test gives p ≈ 0.45. Still very likely chance."
        },
        {
          "from": "charge",
          "text": "The new dressing still looks easier, but I see the numbers aren't moving much."
        }
      ],
      "prompt": "Now what do you decide?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "adopt-wait",
          "text": "Adopt the new dressing because 4 infections is fewer than 7.",
          "quality": "weak",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "icn",
              "text": "But p = 0.45 means the gap is more than likely just noise. We're not learning anything by switching now."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "risk",
              "change": 15
            },
            {
              "meter": "confidence",
              "change": -10
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "chance",
              "kind": "improve",
              "text": "You treated a small difference that is very likely chance as a real effect.",
              "example": "With p = 0.45, you cannot say one dressing is better than the other."
            }
          ],
          "next": "ending-early"
        },
        {
          "id": "ask-sample-again",
          "text": "Ask {{ai}} what sample size we need to detect a meaningful difference.",
          "quality": "strong",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "ai",
              "text": "To detect a drop from 10% to 5% with 80% power, you'd need about 220 per group. That's about 6 more months at this pace."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "risk",
              "change": -10
            },
            {
              "meter": "confidence",
              "change": 15
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": null,
          "notes": [
            {
              "skill": "sample",
              "kind": "good",
              "text": "You asked for the sample size before making a call with weak data.",
              "example": null
            }
          ],
          "next": "sample-size-2"
        },
        {
          "id": "keep-waiting",
          "text": "Tell {{manager}} we should keep collecting data for a few more months.",
          "quality": "fair",
          "replies": [
            {
              "from": "manager",
              "text": "Alright, but set a deadline. We can't study this forever."
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "meter": "risk",
              "change": -5
            },
            {
              "meter": "confidence",
              "change": 5
            }
          ],
          "timeJump": {
            "label": "Six months later",
            "panel": {
              "title": "Infection rates after six more months",
              "metrics": [
                {
                  "label": "Standard dressing",
                  "value": "220 patients, 20 infections",
                  "note": "9.1%"
                },
                {
                  "label": "New dressing",
                  "value": "220 patients, 10 infections",
                  "note": "4.5%"
                }
              ],
              "note": "Gap of 4.6 points; p = 0.04, now significant."
